/-!
# A common controlled endpoint around an actual cusp boundary circle

For each sufficiently small closed tube and each positive norm circle
inside it, one strong deformation retraction of the original quotient
has the independently prescribed collapse as its exact endpoint at
every angle.  The whole-circle prescribed map is jointly continuous in
the original norm-level topology.  On the actual compensated phase
cylinder the endpoint is the literal rotating central-point formula.

The common retraction is chosen after the positive norm is fixed and
before any complex time or angle is selected.  No simultaneous endpoint
prescription at all positive norms is asserted.
-/
